# Nothing here ships in the npm tarball (see package.json "files") or is
# needed to produce it. Every one of these was still sent to the Docker
# daemon and, worse, compiled by `tsc` inside the build stage — tsconfig.json
# includes tests/**, features/** and packages/**/test/** because the same
# config also drives `npm run test:unit` outside Docker. Issue #121: the
# 0.6.0 → 0.7.0 cycle added ~290 files / 35k lines, nearly all of it tests,
# and the arm64 leg of the Docker image build (built under real QEMU emulation on
# an amd64 runner, not Rosetta) went from 3 minutes to a 28-minute cancel.
# Compiling a test suite that never reaches the image should not be on that
# critical path at all, let alone under an emulation penalty.
.git
node_modules
dist
coverage
reports
tests
features
packages/*/test
*.log
